# Mad Mary (docs/voice/mad_mary.md)

~ start
if flag.mad_mary_met
-> again
endif
set mad_mary_met
quest find_gertruda heard
Narrator: A woman in a black shawl rocks in a chair by a cold stove, a girl's dress folded in her lap. She looks up at you with sudden, terrible hope.
Mad Mary [afraid]: Gertruda? Gertruda, is that... no. No, you're not her. Forgive me. You're taller. She's not so tall. She's a good girl.
-> menu

~ again
if flag.gertruda_search_promised
Mad Mary: Have you found her? No. No, you'd have said. You'd have said first thing. Sit, sit. Your sleeve's torn at the seam; leave it with me. I mend things. Everything but the one thing.
else
Mad Mary [sad]: You came back. Nobody comes back. Have you come to look at the mad woman?
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* Who is Gertruda? -> who
* How did she disappear? -> how
* [Insight DC 12] Is she as mad as the village says? -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [if flag.gertruda_window_clue] Mary, her window latch was opened from the inside. -> window
* [if not flag.gertruda_search_promised] We'll look for her. -> promise
* [if not flag.gertruda_search_promised] We can't help you. I'm sorry. -> refuse
* [Cleric] Pray with her for Gertruda. -> pray
* Goodbye. -> END

~ who
Mad Mary: My daughter. Sixteen this spring. Dark hair, like her father. She hums when she's frightened. I kept her in, you see. Sixteen years safe. She never saw the woods, or the castle. She never saw anything.
interject tag:loyal: Sixteen years indoors. That's not a home, that's a garrison.
-> menu

~ how
Mad Mary [sad]: Four nights ago. I went to wake her, and the bed was cold, and the window was open. No blood. The wolves didn't take her; I'd have heard wolves.
Mad Mary [afraid]: There was singing, some nights. Under her window. A man's voice, old songs. I told myself it was the wind. I pulled my own shutters closed.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
Narrator: Under the weeping she is perfectly clear-headed. She isn't mad; she's guilty, and grief is the only thing loud enough to drown it out.
Mad Mary: They call me mad because mad is easier to walk past.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: She rocks, and weeps, and rocks. Whatever is under it, the weeping keeps covered.
-> menu

~ window
quest find_gertruda window_clue
Mad Mary [sad]: From the inside. Then nobody took her. She went to him. Whoever he was, with his old songs. I made a house so safe that a girl had to escape it.
* [Persuasion DC 12] You kept her alive for sixteen years, Mary. That isn't a crime. -> comfort_ok | comfort_fail
* Say nothing for a moment. -> menu

~ comfort_ok
attitude mad_mary friendly
Narrator: The rocking slows. For the first time since you came in, she looks at you and not past you.
Mad Mary: Sixteen years. Yes. That's something. That's something, isn't it. Thank you.
-> menu

~ comfort_fail
Mad Mary [sad]: Kind of you. It's not true, but it's kind. She'd say the same. She's kinder than me, my Gertruda.
-> menu

~ promise
set gertruda_search_promised
quest find_gertruda promised
attitude mad_mary friendly
Mad Mary [afraid]: You will? You'll look? Dark hair, a blue dress with a mended hem, she hums when she's afraid. She'll be afraid. Tell her I'm not angry. Tell her the door is unlocked now. All three locks.
interject name:thistle: Grandda says nobody's lost. Just not found yet. I'll find her.
-> menu

~ refuse
quest find_gertruda refused
Mad Mary: Of course. Of course you can't. Thank you for listening. Nobody listens. Mind the step on your way out; it sticks.
Narrator: Before you reach the door, the weeping starts again, exactly where it left off.
-> END

~ pray
Narrator: You pray aloud for a girl you have never met. Mary doesn't close her eyes; she watches your lips, as if checking the words.
Mad Mary: Do they work, here? Prayers? No, don't answer. Say another one.
-> menu
